menu "Apple"

config SND_SOC_APPLE_MCA
	tristate "Apple Silicon MCA driver"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	select SND_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  This option enables an ASoC platform driver for MCA peripherals found
	  on Apple Silicon SoCs.

config SND_SOC_APPLE_S8000_MCA
	tristate "Apple S8000/T8010 MCA driver"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on COMMON_CLK
	select MFD_SYSCON
	select SND_SOC_GENERIC_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  This option enables an ASoC CPU DAI driver for the "mca-version 4"
	  I2S serializer of the Apple A9 (S8000/S8003), and the version 5
	  serializer of the A10 (T8010). The driver also
	  exports the MCA's MCLK output as a clock for the codec and routes
	  the MCA to its pad in the shared i2s-switch. Samples are moved by
	  SmartIO DMA, so APPLE_SIO_DMA is needed for audio.

	  Say Y or M here if you have an Apple A9 device such as the iPad 5 or iPad 6.

config SND_SOC_APPLE_J71B_DIGITAL
	tristate "Apple J71b reset-held digital audio reference"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF && GPIOLIB && COMMON_CLK && EXPERT
	select SND_SOC_APPLE_S8000_MCA
	help
	  Enable the recovered four-channel, eight-slot J71b MCA2 reference
	  profile and a qualification card that keeps the speaker amplifiers
	  in reset. No board node is enabled. This is not acoustic playback
	  support; electrical timing, channel routing and speaker protection
	  remain unqualified. If unsure, say N.

config SND_SOC_APPLE_T8010_MCA_REFERENCE_KUNIT_TEST
	tristate "Tests for the J71b MCA reference profile" if !KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	depends on KUNIT
	default KUNIT_ALL_TESTS
	help
	  Test the fixed profile's parameter restrictions and register values.
	  The cases cover invalid masks, widths, channels and rates, as well
	  as the recovered frame and serializer register encoding.
	  No hardware or firmware files are accessed.

endmenu
